From: MedyMa <75345465+MedyMa@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt_wifi7: fix missing declarations under GCC 14

The vendor sources use AC_NUM in sr_cmd.h without ensuring that the WMM
access-category count is defined first. They also expose a pointer to
mt_priv_pmksa_info in sta_cfg.h without a prior declaration, which GCC 14
rejects because the build enables -Werror.

Provide the standard four WMM access categories as a guarded fallback and
forward-declare the PMKSA structure before it is used in function prototypes.

--- a/mt_wifi/include/sr_cmd.h
+++ b/mt_wifi/include/sr_cmd.h
@@ -20,6 +20,10 @@
 
 #ifndef __CMM_SR_CMD_H__
 #define __CMM_SR_CMD_H__
+
+#ifndef AC_NUM
+#define AC_NUM 4
+#endif
 
 #ifdef CFG_SUPPORT_FALCON_SR
 /*******************************************************************************
--- a/mt_wifi/include/sta/sta_cfg.h
+++ b/mt_wifi/include/sta/sta_cfg.h
@@ -28,6 +28,8 @@
 
 #ifndef __STA_CFG_H__
 #define __STA_CFG_H__
+
+struct mt_priv_pmksa_info;
 
 INT RTMPSTAPrivIoctlSet(
 	IN RTMP_ADAPTER * pAd,
